    "body": "@domenic: close inspection of the source will show you that I used them in the bug report; so yes, I know browsers currently support the present broken spec; however, the thing that would fix it is precisely if this spec recognised a clear mistake and introduced a backwards-incompatible change.  I sincerely doubt more folk use &amp;larrpl; deliberately for its specified meaning than use it expecting the meaning I suggest (and I'm fairly sure both groups are small, probably empty); and the browsers aren't hand-coding this stuff, they're surely using the ```entities.json``` file or something derived from it to generate their entity mappings, so a fix by WhatWG would soon enough fix all browsers.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
